# counting_divisors:
# CSES 1713, Counting Divisors (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1713), in our
# own words: for each given positive integer number, the number of positive integers
# that divide it. The input is a Scott list (corpora/library/prelude/list) of
# binary naturals (corpora/library/binary/natural) and the answer the Scott
# list of their divisor counts, binary naturals. Part of the CSES port's second
# batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: the divisors of number are the divisor from 1 to
# number with number mod divisor = 0, counted by walking divisor up from 1 with a running count. The
# reading takes number steps, each a division by repeated reduction, for each number; the
# replacement the family asks for is the divisor count from the exponents of the
# prime factorization, with a sieve of the smallest prime factor up to the
# largest number (about the square root of number per query without a sieve).
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application
# only, with no top, no choice and no parallel. It β-reduces to V, the Scott list
# of the canonical binary numerals of the counts (the walk consumes number - divisor, binary_modulo
# consumes the bits of number, each fold a finite list), and binary_modulo is
# given divisor >= 1 only, as ../common/binary_modular needs, and writes no top. So
# ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the soundness of the derivable equations for the
# contextual preorder of Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an
# answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W,
# while Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to
# λx y. y, and applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the
# second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ map _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ binary_odd _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment _ _ merge_binary_equality
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "cses") "common") "binary_modular")
λ _ _ _ binary_modulo
. (λtuple. tuple (binary_odd binary_zero))
λ one
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ number
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self divisor count
        . binary_less_than number divisor count (self (merge_binary_increment divisor) (merge_binary_equality (binary_modulo number divisor) binary_zero (merge_binary_increment count) count))
      ) one binary_zero
  )
λ divisor_count
. (λtuple. tuple λnumbers. map divisor_count numbers)
λ counting_divisors
. export counting_divisors
